# Playwright-ready accessibility (storefront)

When you **add or refactor** interactive UI in this app, make elements easy to target with Playwright’s **locator API** (`getByRole`, `getByLabel`, `getByTestId`) without brittle CSS or duplicate-text hacks.

## Priority (use the first option that works)

1. **Semantic role + accessible name** — `button`, `link`, `textbox`, `combobox`, `dialog` with a visible label, `aria-label`, or associated `<Label htmlFor="…">` / `DialogTitle`.
2. **`data-testid`** — when the control has no stable name (icon-only, repeated Persian copy, link-wrapped button, desktop + mobile duplicates).

Playwright prefers real accessibility first; `data-testid` is for gaps, not a substitute for form labels.

## `data-testid` convention

- kebab-case, flow-scoped: `auth-phone`, `cart-confirm`, `shipping-create-address`, `payment-submit`.
- Put on the **element Playwright clicks** (often the `<a>` or `<button>`, not an inner `<span>`).
- One id per logical control per viewport when mobile/desktop markup diverges (e.g. `cart-confirm-mobile` / `cart-confirm-desktop`) only if both stay in the DOM; otherwise one id on the visible control is enough.

```tsx
<Button data-testid="payment-submit" type="button" onClick={on.handleCreateOrder}>
  <UI_Typography className="reg16">پرداخت</UI_Typography>
</Button>
```

```tsx
<Link href={href} data-testid="cart-confirm" aria-label="ثبت سفارش">
  {buttonContent}
</Link>
```

## Forms and dialogs

- Inputs: keep `id` + `FieldLabel` / `htmlFor` (matches `getByLabel`).
- Modals: keep a clear `DialogTitle` so `getByRole("dialog", { name: "…" })` works (`انتخاب آدرس`, `ثبت اطلاعات شناسایی`, etc.).
- Combobox triggers: ensure an accessible name (label text or `aria-label` on the trigger).

## Do not

- Add `data-testid` to every wrapper `div`.
- Rely on placeholder-only identification for required fields.
- Break shadcn/theme rules for test hooks (no extra color classes; attributes only).
- Remove visible text users need just to simplify tests.

## When touching checkout/auth/profile/shipping/payment/cart

Add or preserve **either** a stable accessible name **or** a `data-testid` on primary actions (submit, pay, add to cart, address save, OTP submit). Update matching specs in `../ecommerce_e2e` in the same change when you rename or split controls.
